"Phase 2 landed (commit b86aec5): incremental strict pushes. The skip-if-populated guard is gone; every push applies. match_names replaces intern_names: existing name -> same id forever, new name -> max+1 (no reuse/reindex), matched bodies rewritten unconditionally; derived rows (action_steps, location_map_connections) rebuilt wholesale. Fail-fast per user rule (no fallbacks, pre-production): omitted existing asset -> Err; omitted registered named entity -> Err; anonymous instantiate blobs on an update push -> Err (must be named to be addressable); unknown refs already Err. Named blobs with existing registration are IMPRINTED onto their entity (component upsert) instead of re-instantiated -- first real use of blob imprinting. new_player special blob updates by key. E2E: assets phase now covers identical re-push, modified re-push with reordered input (id stability proven against enumeration), fresh-id append, body update, and the omission failure (SDK reducer promise rejection carries the Err string). Full gate green. TASK CORE COMPLETE. Remaining nits recorded: explicit asset-removal admin op (future); registry cleanup on entity deletion (future)."